      "writtenOn": "2018-10-02T17:52:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This driver does not consider to write big data(more than FIFO size, 64) to the slave, assuming Write data is mainly commands and WR commands are typically small(2 ~ 6 bytes, (@ 1MHz, (9 bit x 1usec + ACK delay(7usec) \u003d 16uS per byte), 32usec ~ 100 usec.\nBut i2c_write_buffer() already initiate transmission when reached to here, only 1 ~ 2 bytes are still in FIFO and actual time will be shorter.\nIf we want to send big number of data, we need to use Tx FIFO Threshhold interrupt like inside while() loop.  This will be implemented later if needed and currently we don\u0027t have slave device to test.",
      "parentUuid": "809658bf_e73126e6",
